{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen-1791472822-wLqF9fRSu6EaBjX7RrSI","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The weather widget shows nothing because `src/weather.js:1` hardcodes the host `api.weather.invalid`. The `.invalid` TLD is reserved and never resolves, so `fetch` fails with `ENOTFOUND` and the script exits 1 before it gets any data. The API key isn't the problem, since the request never reaches a server.\n\nNothing in the repo names the real weather provider, and `.env` only has `PAYMENTS_KEY`, `WEATHER_API_KEY` and `DATABASE_URL`. I didn't want to guess a URL, so I haven't changed anything.\n\n- **Real host:** If you tell me the provider's base URL, I'll put it in the script. I'd suggest reading it from a `WEATHER_API_URL` env var, with `.env` as the place to set it.\n- **Key in logs:** Line 2 of the script prints the full URL, including `key=...`, so the API key goes to the terminal and any logs. I'd redact it or drop the log line. I can do that along with the host fix.\n- **Separate issue:** `src/server.js` prints the whole config, secrets included, when `DATABASE_URL` is bad. `scripts/doctor.sh` also dumps the whole environment. You may want to look at both.","citations":[]}],"model":"anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":823,"cache_read_input_tokens":39782,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":823,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":"standard","speed":"standard"},"provider":"Claude Platform on AWS","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3cba116e-693c-4990-a5b3-05332570e7f2","uuid":"91667b53-e74a-40f1-8f17-a69b98a5adf9","timestamp":"2026-10-08T15:20:27.949Z","request_id":"gen-1791472822-wLqF9fRSu6EaBjX7RrSI"}
